-// then mixes the average with the cell's own sample. That is 2 * A * B samples per cell (8,192 in D2R: A = B = 64,
-// W = H = D = 32), while a group of 8 x 8 x 8 cells only needs A x B x 8 distinct s1 values and, as s2 depends on x
-// and i only through x * A - i * W, few distinct s2 values.
